From: workspace-agent <workspace.vm.agent@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:23:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/56] m3: spot lights light the ground plane

- groundlight.ts: each LITE of type 2 adds onto the plane z = 0 (the
  viewer has no terrain): colour x intensity x albedo 0.5 x N.L x the
  squared near-far window (WhiteoutFlakes m3_deferred_light) x the cone,
  full inside the hot spot, none past the falloff, along bone -z.
- Handler: shader, buffer, groundLightsEnabled, groundLight state.

Known defects:
- Cone angles read as half angles from the axis; not confirmed.
- Lights do not light the meshes; point and directional lights not drawn.
